  "title": "Register of government contracts",
  "summary": "This page provides information on Service NSW's obligations to record and publish details of government contracts and outlines requirements under various acts.",
  "topics": [
    "government-contracts",
    "nsw-tenders",
    "public-disclosure",
    "service-nsw-contracts"
  ],
  "intro": "All contracts Service NSW (SNSW) enters into with the private sector valued over $150,000 must be recorded in the register of government contracts and published on the NSW Government's eTendering website.\n\nDetails of each contract must be entered into the register within 45 working days of coming into effect, and must remain on the register for 20 business days or until the contract is complete, whichever is longer.\n\nAs required by Premiers Memorandum 2007-01, you will find details of current Service NSW contracts and tender opportunities on eTendering.\n\nThe Government Information (Public Access) Act 2009 (GIPA) requires the publication of a copy of the contract document (minus commercial-in-confidence content) for all class 3 contracts on the agency's website.\n\nYou will find class 3 contracts entered into by Service NSW in the following table.",
